  "text": "The longest river in the world is the Nile River.\n\nRegarding the equation provided:\nx/2 - 1/3 = 3x/4 + 5\n\nTo simplify and solve for x:\n1. Multiply the entire equation by 12 (the least common multiple of 2, 3, and 4) to eliminate fractions:\n   12 * (x/2) - 12 * (1/3) = 12 * (3x/4) + 12 * 5\n   6x - 4 = 9x + 60\n\n2. Rearrange the terms to isolate x:\n   6x - 9x = 60 + 4\n   -3x = 64\n\n3. Solve for x:\n   x = -64/3\n\nThe simplified equation is 6x - 4 = 9x + 60, and the solution is x = -64/3."
